  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 930 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\n07/00Z model and numerical guidance shows the aforementioned \nupper level low eventually moving back northeast across east Texas into\nthe lower Mississippi River Valley by middle of next week. In the\nwake of the mid level disturbance, dry weather conditions will \ncontinue. A pronounced sinusoidal H500 pattern will develop across\nthe western 1/3 CONUS, with a ridge building into the Four \nCorners region by the end of the forecast period, aiding the large\nscale UL subsidence in the region and continued dry conditions. \nTemperatures will be near to slightly above average for early \nNovember.",
